  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 220 PM CDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\nHigh pressure is set up over the central part of the United States. \nThis will bring clear skies and dry weather to IL for the next \nseveral days to a week. Winds have also become very light to near \ncalm. The main focus of this forecast is the temperatures and the \nfrost potential tonight. Temperatures will drop down into the mid \n30s tonight. With clear skies, light winds, and cold temperatures \nfrost formation is favorable in eastern IL, focused east of I-55 \ntonight. If radiational cooling overperform, temperatures could\nget near freezing in some spots. There is a Frost Advisory in \neffect for that area from 1am to 9am tomorrow morning. There \ncould be some very localized, patchy frost that develops in \nwest-central IL in the lowest/coolest spots. \n\nTemperatures will begin a warming trend tomorrow. Highs tomorrow \nwill be in the mid 60s, but by midweek temperatures will be back \nwell above normal with highs in the upper 70s, nearing 80. Normals \nfor this time of year is around 65-69 degrees across central and \nsoutheastern IL.",
